{"tool_name":"seecite","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"seecite","home":"https://github.com/aksenia/SeeCiTe","license":"MIT","summary":"a method to assess CNV calls from SNP arrays using trio data.\n\nSeeCiTe is a novel CNV quality control tool that post-processes output from current CNV calling tools exploiting child-parent trio data to classify calls in quality categories and provide a set of visualizations for each putative CNV call in the offspring. It utilizes probe-level CNV data in trios (and singletons) to systematically highlight potential artefacts and visualize signal intensities in a streamlined fashion suitable for biobank scale studies.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T10:47:03Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-13T17:30:26Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:seecite","credit":[{"email":"ksenia.lavrichenko@gmail.com","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"SNP detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0484"},{"term":"Splitting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3359"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}]}],"name":"SeeCiTe","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.09.28.316372"}],"topic":[{"term":"Biobank","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3337"},{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Microarray experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3518"},{"term":"Probes and primers","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0632"},{"term":"Sequence sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0160"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"SeeCiTe","home":"https://bio.tools/seecite","license":"MIT","summary":"a method to assess CNV calls from SNP arrays using trio data.\n\nSeeCiTe is a novel CNV quality control tool that post-processes output from current CNV calling tools exploiting child-parent t